{
  "about": "M60.8: the vault's own Trash. A delete moves the item to .trash/<stamp>/<path>, its comment sidecar to .trash/<stamp>/.comments/, and writes .trashed.json beside them. A stamp is the UTC second plus four lowercase hex characters. Restore puts both back and refuses to overwrite. A stamp dir with a readable manifest lists when its item is there; one without lists as unreadable when it holds anything but dot-names, and is never restored; a name that is no stamp is never listed or purged. The launch purge moves stamp dirs past keep_days, judged by the stamp, never mtime. Replayed by src-tauri/src/vault/trash.rs and src/lib/mockIpc.test.ts (and src/engine/trash.test.ts for the pure half).",
